# eSIM Support Plan (sms-gateway)

Status: PLAN ONLY — do not implement yet.
Author basis: doc/ESIM的机器软件说明.docx, doc/ESIM指令流程.xlsx, and github.com/estkme-group/lpac.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 1. Background — what the hardware and docs tell us

### 1.1 eSIM machine vs. normal modem pool (from 软件说明.docx)
- An eSIM machine looks like a normal EG25 modem pool, but **each COM port has TWO modes**:
  - **Normal mode** — behaves like today's pool: receives SMS / calls (current app behavior).
  - **eSIM-management mode** — the port CANNOT receive SMS; instead you can read the EID,
    download / activate / deactivate / delete eSIM profiles.
- A port boots in Normal mode.

### 1.2 Mode-switch AT commands (sent over the SAME COM serial port)
| Purpose | Command sequence | Expected | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Detect eSIM machine | `ath?` | reply contains `ESIM` | Run ONCE at init per machine (per xlsx note) |
| Enter eSIM mode | `atl6` → `ath7` | each returns `OK` | A Windows **smart-card device appears** after `ath7` |
| Exit to Normal mode | `atl7` → `ath6` | each returns `OK` | Smart-card device disappears; ICCID now = written eSIM |
| Abnormal recovery | `ath0` | `OK` | Restores factory default; then retry |

### 1.3 Hard constraints (from both docs)
- **Only ONE port machine-wide may be in eSIM mode at a time.** Finish + return a port to
  Normal before operating the next port. => a machine-wide serialization gate is mandatory.
- Detecting whether the machine is an eSIM machine only needs a single `ath?` at init.

### 1.4 Canonical provisioning flow (from 指令流程.xlsx)
```
1  COMx  ath?                         -> confirm ESIM machine (once)
2  COMx  atl6
3  COMx  ath7                         -> enter eSIM management (smartcard appears)
4  CLI   lpac profile download <...>  -> download eSIM profile
5  CLI   lpac profile enable <ICCID>  -> activate eSIM
6  COMx  atl7
7  COMx  ath6                         -> exit eSIM management
8  COMx  (normal SMS reception)       -> ICCID is now the eSIM's ICCID
```

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 2. lpac integration facts (from lpac USAGE / ENVVARS / backends docs)

- lpac is a C CLI (`lpac <subcommand> [subcommand2] [params]`) implementing SGP.22 LPA.
- **All output is JSON**: `{"type":"lpa","payload":{"code":0,"message":"success","data":...}}`
  - `code==0` = success; otherwise error code. `message` = "success" or error text.
- Subcommands we need:
  - `chip info` — EID + default SM-DP+/SM-DS.
  - `profile list | enable <ICCID/AID> [1/0] | disable <ICCID/AID> [1/0] | delete <ICCID> | nickname <ICCID> <name>`
  - `profile download -s <smdp> -m <matchingId> [-c <conf>] [-i <imei>] [-a <LPA:1$smdp$matchingId>]`
  - `notification list | process [-a] [-r] <seq> | remove [-a] <seq>` (GSMA requires processing).
- **APDU backend selection (env vars):**
  - `LPAC_APDU=pcsc` (DEFAULT, recommended here): talks to the Windows smart-card reader
    that appears in eSIM mode. Select reader via `LPAC_APDU_PCSC_DRV_NAME=<name>` or
    `LPAC_APDU_PCSC_DRV_IFID=<index>`. Enumerate with `lpac driver apdu`.
  - `LPAC_APDU=at` / `at_csim` + `LPAC_APDU_AT_DEVICE=COMx`: APDU over the serial port itself.
    lpac docs mark this **"FOR DEMO PURPOSES ONLY"** — 300 ms max response time, download/delete
    often fail, and it would need EXCLUSIVE serial access (conflicts with our open handle).
    => **Do NOT use the AT backend for real provisioning; PC/SC is the supported path.**
  - `LPAC_HTTP=winhttp` on Windows (or `curl`).
- **Key architectural consequence:** mode-switching uses the serial port; the eUICC/profile
  work uses a SEPARATE PC/SC smart-card channel. Our Rust app can keep its serial handle open;
  it just must PAUSE SMS activity on that port while in eSIM mode. Because only one port is ever
  in eSIM mode, exactly ONE smart-card reader is present at a time — trivial to target.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 3. Design decisions

- D1. Use **lpac.exe (PC/SC backend)** as an external process; wrap + parse its JSON. Do not
  reimplement SGP.22.
- D2. **Machine-wide async gate** (`tokio::sync::Mutex` or a single-permit `Semaphore`) serializes
  all eSIM sessions. A session = enter → operations → exit, held for the whole span.
- D3. Add a **per-port operational mode** (`Normal` | `EnteringEsim` | `EsimManaging` | `Exiting`).
  Existing SMS/recheck/URC workers must skip a port unless mode == `Normal`.
- D4. **RAII session guard**: acquiring a session returns a guard that, on drop/error/panic,
  ALWAYS attempts `atl7`→`ath6` (and `ath0` if abnormal) and releases the gate — so a port can
  never get stuck in eSIM mode.
- D5. **Reuse the existing serial channel** (`Modem::send_command`) for `ath?/atl6/ath7/atl7/ath6/ath0`.
  No second serial opener.
- D6. After exiting eSIM mode, **trigger a re-init/recheck of that port** so the SMS side re-reads
  the (possibly new) ICCID/IMSI and resumes receiving on the activated profile.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 4. Data model / migrations (migrations/2026XXXX_esim.sql)

- `esim_capable_ports` (or add columns to existing port/modem tracking):
  - `com_port TEXT PRIMARY KEY`, `eid TEXT`, `is_esim_capable INTEGER`, `updated_at`.
- `esim_profiles` (cache of `lpac profile list`, keyed to a port/EID):
  - `id`, `com_port`, `eid`, `iccid`, `isdp_aid`, `profile_state` (enabled/disabled),
    `nickname`, `service_provider_name`, `profile_name`, `profile_class`, `updated_at`.
- `esim_operations` (audit log):
  - `id`, `com_port`, `eid`, `op_type` (detect/enter/exit/reset/download/enable/disable/delete/nickname),
    `params_json`, `result_code`, `message`, `created_at`.
- Migrations follow existing naming (see migrations/README.md and prior `2026...` files).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 5. Config additions (src/config.rs `Settings`, all optional/back-compat)

- `esim_enabled: Option<bool>`                (default false)
- `lpac_exe: Option<String>`                  (path to lpac.exe)
- `lpac_apdu_backend: Option<String>`         (default "pcsc")
- `lpac_http_backend: Option<String>`         (default "winhttp")
- `lpac_pcsc_reader_name: Option<String>`     (optional fixed reader name)
- `esim_default_smdp: Option<String>`         (fallback SM-DP+)
- `esim_state_switch_timeout_secs: Option<u64>` (default ~10)
- `esim_reader_settle_ms: Option<u64>`        (wait after ath7 for smartcard to appear, default ~1500)
- Per-`Device`: optional `esim_capable: Option<bool>` manual override.
- Document all in config.toml.example.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 6. Backend module design (new: src/esim/)

- `src/esim/mod.rs`      — public surface: `EsimService` handle wired into main.rs + ModemManager.
- `src/esim/state.rs`    — `PortMode` enum, machine-wide gate, `EsimSession` RAII guard
                           (enter/exit sequences via `Modem::send_command`, error recovery `ath0`).
- `src/esim/lpac.rs`     — spawn lpac with the right env (`LPAC_APDU`, `LPAC_HTTP`,
                           `LPAC_APDU_PCSC_DRV_NAME/IFID`); typed wrappers:
                           `chip_info`, `profile_list`, `download`, `enable`, `disable`, `delete`,
                           `nickname`, `notification_*`; JSON envelope parse -> `Result<T, LpacError>`.
- `src/esim/reader.rs`   — enumerate PC/SC readers via `lpac driver apdu`; pick the single present
                           reader (or configured name) while in eSIM mode.
- ModemManager integration:
  - Add `esim_capable` + `mode: RwLock<PortMode>` to `Modem` (src/modem/core.rs) OR a side map in
    manager keyed by com_port.
  - At init: after successful modem init, run `ath?` once; set `esim_capable` if reply has `ESIM`.
  - Gate SMS read loop, recheck/demotion worker, URC handlers, and hot-swap probe on
    `mode == Normal` so an eSIM-mode port is NOT demoted or read.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 7. API endpoints (src/api/mod.rs, prefix /api/esim, admin-auth like the rest)

- `GET  /api/esim/ports`                     — list eSIM-capable ports, mode, EID, gate status.
- `POST /api/esim/{com}/session/enter`       — acquire gate + atl6/ath7 (returns session state).
- `POST /api/esim/{com}/session/exit`        — atl7/ath6 + release gate + trigger port re-init.
- `POST /api/esim/{com}/reset`               — ath0 recovery.
- `GET  /api/esim/{com}/chip`                — lpac chip info (EID, default SM-DP+).
- `GET  /api/esim/{com}/profiles`            — lpac profile list (also refresh DB cache).
- `POST /api/esim/{com}/profiles/download`   — body {smdp, matching_id, confirmation_code, imei, activation_code}.
- `POST /api/esim/{com}/profiles/enable`     — {iccid, refresh_flag?}.
- `POST /api/esim/{com}/profiles/disable`    — {iccid, refresh_flag?}.
- `POST /api/esim/{com}/profiles/delete`     — {iccid} (audit; no auto-confirm in UI is dangerous).
- `POST /api/esim/{com}/profiles/nickname`   — {iccid, nickname}.
- `GET/POST /api/esim/{com}/notifications*`  — list/process(-r)/remove (GSMA compliance).
- `POST /api/esim/{com}/provision`           — convenience: enter → download → enable → (process
                                               notifications) → exit, all under one gate
                                               (mirrors the xlsx flow).
- All mutating calls append to `esim_operations`. Non-Normal ports should be excluded from the
  normal /api/sims/info "SIM removed" logic (show an "eSIM mode" state instead).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 8. Frontend (frontend/src/pages/EsimManager.svelte + i18n)

- New page/tab "eSIM Manager":
  - Table of eSIM-capable ports: com_port, mode badge (Normal / eSIM mode), EID, current ICCID.
  - Global banner showing the one-at-a-time lock (which port currently holds the eSIM session).
  - Per-port panel (only usable while that port holds the session):
    - Enter / Exit eSIM mode buttons (Exit also on page-leave guard).
    - Profile list table: provider, name, ICCID, state; actions enable/disable/delete/nickname.
    - Download form: SM-DP+ address, matching ID / activation code, confirmation code, IMEI,
      or a single `LPA:1$...$...` activation-code / QR field.
  - Clear warning: "This port stops receiving SMS while in eSIM mode."
- Add i18n keys (EN + ZH) in frontend/src/js/i18n.js.
- Remember: frontend changes require `pnpm build` (frontend) AND `cargo run` recompile
  (RustEmbed) to appear.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 9. Concurrency, safety, and edge cases

- Machine-wide single active eSIM session (gate). Queue or reject concurrent requests with 409.
- RAII guard guarantees return-to-Normal on any error/panic; `ath0` fallback if atl7/ath6 fail.
- Reader-appearance timeout after `ath7` -> `ath0`, abort, release gate, surface error.
- `enable` quirks: per lpac note, some eUICC need AID vs ICCID and refreshFlag 1/0 — expose the
  flag and try fallback ordering.
- `delete` has no secondary confirm in lpac -> require explicit UI confirmation + audit.
- Notifications are NOT auto-sent by lpac -> process (optionally `-r`) after download/enable/delete.
- HTTP egress: `profile download`/`discovery` need internet to the SM-DP+/SM-DS -> document
  firewall/proxy; surface network errors distinctly from card errors.
- Do NOT let recheck/demotion treat an eSIM-mode port as "SIM removed".
- `+CME ERROR: 3` on AT backend is a known modem-setting issue (another reason to prefer PC/SC).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 10. Testing

- Unit: lpac JSON envelope parsing (success + non-zero code + empty data); `PortMode` transitions
  with a mocked `send_command`; gate serialization (second acquire blocks/queues).
- Mock: extend src/modem/mock_manager.rs with an esim-capable fake port + fake profile list so the
  UI and API can be exercised without hardware.
- Hardware runbook (manual): follow §1.4 flow on COM1/COM2; verify smartcard appears/disappears,
  ICCID reflects the eSIM after exit, and SMS resumes.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 11. Phased rollout / milestones

- M1  Detection: `ath?` at init, `esim_capable` flag, `/api/esim/ports`, read-only UI list.
- M2  Session state machine + gate + RAII guard (enter/exit/reset) with SMS workers gated.
- M3  lpac wrapper (chip info + profile list, read-only) end-to-end via PC/SC.
- M4  Mutating ops: download, enable, disable, delete, nickname + notifications + audit log.
- M5  Full UI (download form, actions), i18n, one-at-a-time banner.
- M6  `/api/esim/{com}/provision` one-shot flow + post-exit port re-init + polish/tests.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 12. Open questions / risks (confirm before M1)

- Q1. lpac.exe distribution: bundle a pinned build alongside the app, or require operator install?
      (lpac has its own license — verify redistribution terms.)
- Q2. Confirm the PC/SC reader name pattern this hardware exposes in eSIM mode (for a fixed
      `LPAC_APDU_PCSC_DRV_NAME`); single-reader-at-a-time assumption should make this optional.
- Q3. Does entering eSIM mode on one port disturb neighbors on the same USB hub? (Serialize; test.)
- Q4. Multi-profile eSIM (4 profiles in one eUICC) management UX — list/enable-switch expectations.
- Q5. Whether to auto-process notifications with `-r` by default (GSMA compliance vs. audit needs).
